    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100">

                <pb facs="0173" n="173" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg173"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Lyons to Mr.
                            Seward</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 17, 1861</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to offer you my thanks for the note
                    dated the 14th instant, which you have done me the honor to write to me in
                    answer to that dated the 12th instant, which I addressed to you on the subject
                    of transmitting official correspondence by her Majesty’s ships of war to the
                    blockaded ports.</p>
                <p>It is with reluctance that I importune you further in this matter. But as I am
                    very anxious to avoid all risk of misapprehending your wishes, I venture <pb
                        facs="0174" n="174" xml:id="pg174"/> to ask you whether I am right in
                    understanding that you have no objection to my sending to the blockaded ports,
                    by her Majesty’s ships of war, not only British official correspondence with
                    British authorities, but also the official correspondence of other powers
                    friendly to the United States, with the agents of the same powers in the
                    southern States.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your most obedient, humble
                    servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
